<div class="wrap">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Photography &amp; illustrations</span>
  </nav>
</div>

<section class="wrap wrap-mid" style="padding-bottom:clamp(60px,8vw,110px)">
  <span class="eyebrow">Attribution &amp; disclosure</span>
  <h1 style="margin:14px 0 18px">Photography &amp; illustrations</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every image on this site is one of two things, and which one it is is stated on the image itself.
    <strong class="gold">Photographs</strong> are openly-licensed images used under the terms of their licences;
    Creative Commons requires that the author and the licence are credited, so all of them are listed here.
    <strong class="gold">Illustrations</strong> are drawn for the shop and stand in for pieces we have not
    photographed yet — they are not likenesses of any specific item, and no photograph is borrowed to
    represent them.
  </p>

  <div class="panel" style="margin-top:28px">
    <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">How to tell them apart</h3>
    <div class="stack-12" style="color:var(--text-dim);line-height:1.85;font-size:0.92rem">
      <p>A product whose image is an illustration carries a mark reading
        <span class="illus-mark" style="position:static;display:inline-flex;vertical-align:middle">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 19l7-7 3 3-7 7-3-3z"/><path d="M18 13l-1.5-7.5L2 4l1.5 14.5L11 20l7-7z"/><path d="M2 4l5.5 5.5"/></svg>
          Illustration
        </span> on the image, and a note under the gallery on its product page. The illustration itself also
        carries the words <span class="mono tiny">ILLUSTRATION · PHOTOGRAPHY PENDING</span>, so the disclosure
        travels with the file even if the image is saved or shared elsewhere.</p>
      <p>A product with no such mark is shown with a photograph of that kind of tea or piece of work, credited below.</p>
      <p>Where several lots of one tea are listed — the same Longjing at three picking grades, say — they share that
        tea's photograph, because the photograph shows the tea and the grade is a difference in the picking window
        rather than a different leaf. The product page for each lot says so.</p>
      <p>Where a listing is illustrated and you want to see the actual piece before buying, write to us and we
        will photograph the one in stock and send you its weight and measurements.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="alert alert-info" style="margin-top:28px">
    <strong>A note for whoever takes this site live.</strong> The photographs are real, correctly-licensed
    work, which is why they are safe to ship — but they are not photographs of the exact items this shop
    sells, and the illustrated listings stand in for stock that has not been photographed at all. The whole
    catalogue is seed data: replace it with your own goods and your own photography, drop the files into
    <span class="mono">public/img/photos/</span>, and this page shrinks to the credits that still apply.
  </div>

  <div class="panel" style="margin-top:28px">
    <div class="row-between" style="margin-bottom:18px">
      <h3 style="margin:0"><%= photoCredits.length %> credited images</h3>
      <a class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost" href="/terms#privacy">Privacy &amp; terms</a>
    </div>

    <% if (!photoCredits.length) { %>
      <p class="muted small">No credits recorded yet. Run <span class="mono">npm run photos</span> to build them.</p>
    <% } else { %>
      <div class="credits">
        <% photoCredits.forEach(credit => { %>
          <div class="credits-row">
            <span>
              <% if (credit.source) { %>
                <a href="<%= credit.source %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><%= credit.title || credit.slot %></a>
              <% } else { %>
                <%= credit.title || credit.slot %>
              <% } %>
              <div class="tiny faint mono" style="margin-top:3px"><%= credit.slot %></div>
            </span>
            <span><%= credit.author || 'Unknown author' %><% if (credit.via) { %><br /><span class="tiny faint">via <%= credit.via %></span><% } %></span>
            <span>
              <% if (credit.licenceUrl) { %>
                <a href="<%= credit.licenceUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"><%= credit.licence %></a>
              <% } else { %>
                <%= credit.licence %>
              <% } %>
            </span>
          </div>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</section>
